use std
use amni-drive
into cockpit_render.amni
lang amni
Amni-Drive's Helium + Gold software cockpit renderer with true concave-arc crescent wings (SDF Boolean subtraction of the central circular map), crisp spandrel corner badges (Speed + Sun/Weather icon + Clock), and primary interactive focus. Renders any `layout::CockpitPlan` and `look::Palette` into an RGBA byte buffer (`w * h * 4` bytes).
Struct `Canvas` holds `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers and `px` as a growable byte buffer of length `w * h * 4`.
Function `new_canvas` takes `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers and `bg` as an unsigned 32-bit ARGB color, returning a `Canvas` filled with `bg`.
Function `blend_px` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `x` and `y` as 32-bit integers, `col` as an unsigned 32-bit ARGB color, and `cov` as a 32-bit float coverage in 0 through 1. Alpha-blend R, G, B over destination pixel, keeping alpha 255.
Function `sdf_round_rect` takes `px`, `py`, `x`, `y`, `w`, `h`, and `radius` as 32-bit floats and returns the signed distance to the rounded rectangle (negative inside, positive outside).
Function `fill_round_rect` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `x`, `y`, `w`, `h`, and `radius` as 32-bit floats, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float, and draws an anti-aliased filled rounded rectangle with optional border stroke.
Function `fill_crescent_pod` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `r` as `layout::Rect`, `radius` as a 32-bit float, `cutout` as `layout::Circle`, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float. For every pixel in `r` expanded by 2 pixels, compute `d_box = sdf_round_rect(px, py, r.x, r.y, r.w, r.h, radius)`. When `cutout.r` is greater than 0, compute `d_hole = cutout.r - hypot(px - cutout.cx, py - cutout.cy)` and take `d = max(d_box, d_hole)` (exact concave-arc Boolean subtraction!). Otherwise `d = d_box`. Fill with anti-aliased coverage `clamp(0.5 - d, 0.0, 1.0)` and stroke the entire outer + concave inner arc rim where `d` is between `-stroke_w - 0.5` and `0.5`.
Function `fill_circle_pod` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `cx`, `cy`, and `r` as 32-bit floats, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float, and `ticks` as a boolean. Draw anti-aliased filled circle + border ring; when `ticks` is true draw 36 radial compass ticks around the inner rim (`r - 10` to `r - 3`, longer every 90 degrees) in `stroke`.
Function `fill_hex_pod` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `x`, `y`, `w`, `h`, and `cut` as 32-bit floats, `fill` and `stroke` as unsigned 32-bit colors, and `stroke_w` as a 32-bit float, drawing an anti-aliased 8-vertex chamfered octagon with border stroke.
Function `draw_sun_icon` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `cx`, `cy`, and `r` as 32-bit floats, and `col` as an unsigned 32-bit color; draws a crisp filled sun core circle (`r * 0.48`) with 8 radial rays around it so weather renders as a clean glanceable icon next to the temperature.
Function `glyph_rows` takes an ASCII byte `ch` and returns a 64-bit unsigned integer packing a 5-wide by 7-tall bitmap for A through Z, 0 through 9, space, colon, dot, dash, slash, plus, and `<`/`>`. Map lowercase `a`..`z` to uppercase.
Function `draw_text` takes a mutable `Canvas` `c`, `text` as a read-only byte slice, `x` and `y` as 32-bit floats, `scale` as a 32-bit integer (minimum 1), `col` as an unsigned 32-bit color, and `center_x` as a boolean.
Function `draw_cockpit` takes `w` and `h` as 32-bit integers, `preset_key` as a read-only byte slice, `layout_id` and `dock_mode` as 32-bit integers, `speed_mph` as a 32-bit integer, `temp_f` as a 32-bit integer, and `active_btn` as a 32-bit integer (1..6), returning a `Canvas`.
Use `look::build_palette(preset_key, 0, false)`, `look::car_type_scale(f32(w), f32(h), 1.0)`, and `layout::compute_cockpit(f32(w), f32(h), ts.min_hit_px, ts.gutter_px, ts.pad_px, layout_id, dock_mode, false)`.
1. Create canvas filled with `pal.bg`.
2. Draw `plan.dock_rect` as a rounded container (`radius = 18`, fill `pal.panel`, stroke `pal.line`, `stroke_w = 1.5`).
3. Draw each of the 6 buttons in `plan.buttons` (`"NAV"`, `"MEDIA"`, `"APPS"`, `"VOICE"`, `"VIEW"`, `"SET"`). For button 4 (`VOICE`), draw an accent-ringed circular/pill orb (`stroke = pal.acc`, `stroke_w = 2.5`). For active button (`b.id` equals `active_btn`), fill `pal.acc` with high-contrast text (`0xFF05070A` if dark else `0xFFFFFFFF`); otherwise fill `pal.panel2` with `pal.line` stroke and `pal.ink` text.
4. Draw all pods in `plan.pods` in two passes: first primary panels (`kind` 0, 1, or crescent wings), then secondary badges (`kind` 2, 3, 4, 5) on top so badges sit crisply in their spandrel corners:
   - Shape 1 (circle): `fill_circle_pod` at `pod.circle`, stroke `pal.acc` when `pod.kind` is 0 else `pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 2.2`, `ticks` true when `pod.kind` is 0.
   - Shape 2 (hex): `fill_hex_pod` at `pod.rect` with `pod.chamfer`, stroke `pal.acc` when `pod.kind` is 0 else `pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 2.0`.
   - Shape 3 (capsule): `fill_round_rect` at `pod.rect` with `pod.chamfer`, fill `pal.panel` (or `pal.panel2` for secondary badges `kind >= 2`), stroke `pal.acc` when `pod.kind` is 0 else `pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 1.6`.
   - Shape 4, 5, or 6 (concave crescent wing): `fill_crescent_pod` at `pod.rect`, `pod.chamfer`, `pod.cutout`, fill `pal.panel`, stroke `pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 2.0`.
   - Otherwise (rect): `fill_round_rect` at `pod.rect` with radius 22, fill `pal.panel`, stroke `pal.acc` when `pod.kind` is 0 else `pal.line2`, `stroke_w = 1.6`.
   - Draw crisp glanceable content inside each pod:
     - `kind` 0 (map): subtle road grid lines in `pal.panel2`, bold route chevron in `pal.acc`, `"AMNI-MAP 3D"`, and `"HEADING UP"` in `pal.soft`.
     - `kind` 1 (media): compute visual content center shifted slightly away from any concave `cutout` (if `shape` is 5 `crescent_right`, center horizontally at `pod.rect.x + pod.rect.w * 0.58`; if `shape` is 6 `crescent_bottom`, center vertically at `pod.rect.y + pod.rect.h * 0.58`; else center of `pod.safe_rect`). Draw circular album-art puck with `pal.acc` ring, `"SPOTIFY"`, `"NIGHT DRIVE"`, and wide `<<  PLAY  >>` transport bar with `pal.acc` play pill.
     - `kind` 2 (speed_badge): if `shape` is 4 (`crescent_left`), center content in the left uncarved half (`pod.rect.x + pod.rect.w * 0.42`) and draw large bold speed number (`speed_mph`, scale `max(4, int(ts.telemetry_px / 9.0))`) in `pal.ink` above `"MPH"` in `pal.acc`. Otherwise (compact spandrel capsule), draw bold `speed_mph` + `" MPH"` centered cleanly on one line!
     - `kind` 3 (weather_badge): draw `draw_sun_icon` on the left side of the pill in `pal.gold` and formatted `temp_f` + `"F"` in `pal.ink` right beside it!
     - `kind` 4 (apps_badge): draw `"APPS"` + 4 accent dots.
     - `kind` 5 (clock_badge): draw `"11:45 PM"` centered in `pal.soft`.
Function `write_ppm` writes binary P6 PPM to `path`.
Function `main` renders four updated preview images into `/tmp/amni_he_preview/`:
1. `honda_800x480_twin_chrono.ppm` (800 by 480, `"amni_dark"`, layout 0, dock 0, speed 65, temp 72, active 1)
2. `car_1280x720_solar_orbit.ppm` (1280 by 720, `"amni_dark"`, layout 1, dock 0, speed 68, temp 72, active 1)
3. `car_1280x720_hex_light.ppm` (1280 by 720, `"amni_light"`, layout 4, dock 0, speed 45, temp 74, active 2)
4. `portrait_720x1280_capsule.ppm` (720 by 1280, `"high_contrast"`, layout 1, dock 1, speed 55, temp 68, active 1)
Print `"rendered 4 concave helium previews ok"` when done.
